# What NOT to upload.
#
# Read this as a denylist and mean it: Vercel publishes the repository root, so
# anything absent from this file is on the public internet. That is the opposite
# of how the old Cloudflare script worked — it named the files that belonged in
# the deploy, and everything else was excluded by default. Adding a directory to
# the repository now means deciding whether it ships.
#
# What does ship: the marketing pages, `assets/`, the built editor in `app/`,
# `api/` for the auth function, and the files a host reads from the site root
# (robots.txt, sitemap.xml, site.webmanifest, vercel.json).

# Source. The editor is committed pre-built in app/, so the builder itself is
# never needed at deploy time — see docs/DEPLOY.md.
builder
legacy

# Build tooling and the artwork it consumes. design/ holds the 1.3 MB logo
# master, which exists to regenerate assets/images/* and has no business being
# fetched by a visitor.
scripts
design

# Documentation and database schema. Neither is secret, and neither is a page.
docs
neon
README.md

# Editor and agent configuration.
.kiro
.claude
.github
.vscode

# Noise. .DS_Store in particular lists filenames that are nobody else's business.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
